# URL contract for vendored static assets — reference document
#
# T4's server.go mounts this directory at /ui/static/ via
# http.FileServer(http.FS(staticSubFS)) + http.StripPrefix.
# T6's templates emit <link>/<script> URLs against the paths below.
# Reverse-proxy operators (nginx, Caddy) can mirror these headers in
# front of regatta serve without changing application code.
#
# Format: one line per asset.
#   <url-path>  <content-type>  <cache-control>

/ui/static/tailwind.min.css  text/css; charset=utf-8         public, max-age=86400, immutable
/ui/static/htmx.min.js       application/javascript; charset=utf-8  public, max-age=86400, immutable

# Notes:
# - immutable + 1-day max-age is safe because every URL is content-pinned
#   by SHA-256 in VENDORED.md; a byte change ships under the same path
#   but lands behind a release tag, so cache-bust is per-deploy.
# - CSP (T4's csp.go) restricts script-src + style-src to 'self'; these
#   URLs are the only satisfier. Add no external origins here.
# - Asset paths are stable across waves. If a future task renames a
#   file, update this contract AND every template reference in the same
#   PR — the rename is a wire-format break.
